--- body ---
## Context

0929 fixes the close-claim extraction regex in `skills/merge/erg-pr-merge` and
in `skills/roar/check-close-claims.sh`. git-erg 0255 fixes the same defect in
its own copy. Three independent point fixes to one grammar is exactly the shape
that drifts back apart: nothing today asserts that the copies accept the same
PR-body forms, and the defect survived from 2026-05-23 (the original GitHub
issue #145) to 2026-09-16 unnoticed in all three.

The `check-close-claims.sh` instance is why this ticket is not optional. That
script is the field detector for dropped claims, and it shared the defect --
so the one mechanism that would have caught the drift was itself blind to it.

This is a `/roar` step 4 follow-up, filed because the sweep was juicy -- two
instances of one anti-pattern -- and per that step the test is deliberately NOT
bundled into 0929's fix PR. A per-PR gate catches the bug being reintroduced in
the file under review; a standing test is what catches the class coming back in
an unrelated future PR.

## Relevant files

- `skills/merge/erg-pr-merge` -- the extraction under test
- `skills/roar/check-close-claims.sh` -- the field detector, which should keep
  agreeing with the extraction about what counts as a claim
- `tests/` -- wherever the harness's shell-level tests live; follow the existing
  convention rather than inventing a new harness

## Actions

1. Write a table-driven test over PR-body fixtures: open path, closed path, the
   three `Ticket:` spellings, multiple claims in one body, no claim at all, and
   a body that mentions `tickets/` in prose without a claim line.
2. Assert the extraction and `check-close-claims.sh` agree on every fixture --
   the two must not disagree about what a claim is, or the detector will report
   phantom DROPPED findings.
3. Decide and record whether git-erg's `tickets/erg-github` copy is in scope for
   a cross-repo assertion, or whether each repo tests its own copy against a
   shared fixture list. Prefer the shared fixture list: a cross-repo test needs a
   checkout it cannot assume.

## Test

This ticket *is* the test. The red step is that the fixture list must include at
least one case that fails against the pre-0929 extraction, so the suite
demonstrates it can see the defect it exists to prevent -- a fixture set that
passes against both the broken and the fixed regex is a vacuous control.

## Verification

- [ ] Running the new test against the pre-0929 `erg-pr-merge` fails
- [ ] Running it against the post-0929 `erg-pr-merge` passes
- [ ] The test runs in whatever `make` target CI already invokes, not only by hand

## Invariants

- No change to `erg-pr-merge` behaviour in this ticket; 0929 owns the fix.
- The test must not require a forge, a network call, or a real PR.

## Exit criteria

- A standing test covers the close-claim grammar, fails against the old
  extraction, and runs in CI
- The fixture list is written down in one place both copies can be checked
  against
